WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.740
Toss a coin to your new Witcher! If&nbsp;
you've been struggling to imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.180
Liam Hemsworth as Geralt of Rivia, some&nbsp;
stunning new fan art is here to help.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.660
When "The Witcher" premiered&nbsp;
on Netflix in late 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.980
fans of the popular novels and video&nbsp;
games were treated to largely faithful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.180
storytelling and an accurate visual&nbsp;
representation of the source material.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.340
The series tells the tale of Geralt, the&nbsp;
namesake Witcher, a lover of baths and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.620
slayer of all manner of gnarly beasts. Although&nbsp;
some fans felt Season 1's multiple timelines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.300
made it needlessly confusing, the show has&nbsp;
received generally good reviews for its CGI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.400
acting, and a second season that many fans&nbsp;
felt was a clear improvement over the first.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.040
"Took me to the fourth verse to&nbsp;
understand there were different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.300
timelines." "Oh did it? Wow." "And&nbsp;
that magic kiss? That was a bit cheap."

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.720
Season 3 of "The Witcher" has&nbsp;
been filmed, but with the news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.740
that Henry Cavill is being recast with&nbsp;
Liam Hemsworth as Geralt for Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.000
many fans are both displeased and&nbsp;
apprehensive about the show's future.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.200
The English actor embodied the role&nbsp;
with the commanding presence, humor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.520
and charisma that he has become known for.&nbsp;
So it is only natural for viewers to feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.900
disappointment once the actor they are&nbsp;
familiar with exits a program. But with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.280
some fan art already bringing Hemsworth to&nbsp;
life as Geralt, the future looks promising.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.900
Digital artist royy_ledger shared an image&nbsp;
on his Instagram page that gives fans a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.700
fun "preview" of what the Australian actor&nbsp;
could look like in the part. With Geralt's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.600
signature yellow eyes and white hair and&nbsp;
beard, Hemsworth appears to fit the bill.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.080
Hemsworth let fans know on&nbsp;
Instagram that he's pumped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.620
to portray Geralt in Season 4&nbsp;
and beyond, posting, in part,

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.000
"As a Witcher fan I'm over the moon&nbsp;
about the opportunity to play Geralt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.420
of Rivia. I'm truly excited to be&nbsp;
stepping into The Witcher world."

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.640
Despite his excitement, fan discourse is mixed&nbsp;
with much of the dismay stemming from Cavill's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.560
leaving the part so many have become familiar&nbsp;
with through him. Over on Reddit, one fan posted,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.720
"Well, at this point, after seeing Henry, who can&nbsp;
say anyone else will ever be right for this role?"

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.660
Another fan reaffirmed this sentiment by replying,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.940
"Honestly, at this moment there's no actor on this&nbsp;
planet that is right for Geralt. (Except Cavill)."

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.100
Like his predecessor, Liam Hemsworth is no&nbsp;
stranger to action/adventure movie franchises.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.800
"It is wonderful to see you again."

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.620
The Australian actor starred as Gale&nbsp;
Hawthorne in "The Hunger Games" franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.540
in addition to lead roles in "Independence&nbsp;
Day: Resurgence" and "The Duel." In his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.680
Instagram post, Hemsworth shouted out Cavill,&nbsp;
acknowledging that he has big boots to fill:

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.480
"Henry Cavill has been an incredible Geralt,&nbsp;
and I'm honored that he's handing me the reins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.580
and allowing me to take up the White Wolf's blades&nbsp;
for the next chapter of his adventure. Henry, I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.900
been a fan of yours for years and was inspired&nbsp;
by what you brought to this beloved character."

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.380
Meanwhile, Hemsworth received the&nbsp;
seal of approval from the "Man of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.200
Steel" star himself. On Instagram, Cavill shared,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.721
"In my stead, the fantastic Mr. Liam Hemsworth&nbsp;
will be taking up the mantle of the White Wolf."

